firing 2: {"ts": "2026-11-19T09:31:34Z", "build_log_compiling": true, "sweep_stdout": "{\"verb\": \"run\", \"outcome\": \"refused\", \"cause\": \"build-in-flight\"}", "sweep_exit": 3, "deps_before": 2006, "deps_after": 2024, "deps_removed": 2, "removed_names_shape": ["futures_concurrency-H.futures_concurrency.H-cgu.0.rcgu.o", "rmetaNgCDFz"]}
reading: refused · exit 3 · the sweep removed nothing (its refusal path runs no keep pass and no removal). The deps count is not constant across the call because the in-flight build adds files and rustc renames its own transients (a codegen object, a temp rmeta directory) — the names that vanished are those transients, none a unit name.
lock premise: measured on cargo 1.99.0 — a scratch crate's build held target/debug/.cargo-lock, .cargo-build-lock and .cargo-artifact-lock (flock EWOULDBLOCK) for its length, all three free after it.
